          "properties": {
            "severity": "critical",
            "security-severity": "9.8",
            "cvssRating": "Critical",
            "category": "CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials",
            "cvssVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
            "cwe": "CWE-798 - Use of Hard-coded Credentials",
            "cweId": "CWE-798",
            "cweName": "Use of Hard-coded Credentials",
            "cvssScore": 9.8,
            "offensivePriority": "P4",
            "offensivePriorityLabel": "Code-Knowledge / Insider Dependent",
            "offensivePriorityReason": "Code-Knowledge / Insider Dependent | *requires source-code / insider knowledge*",
            "confidence": 0.95,
            "description": "#### Description\nThe cookieSecret configuration value is a static string in config/env/all.js and is used as the express-session secret. This allows anyone with access to the repository to sign arbitrary session cookies, bypassing authentication entirely.\n\n#### Impact\nAn attacker who obtains the hardcoded session secret from the source code can forge valid session cookies for any user, including administrators, leading to complete account takeover and data breach.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAn attacker reads the publicly available source code to obtain the cookieSecret. They then craft a session cookie containing a desired userId and the correct signature. Sending this cookie to the application grants them access as that user, including admin privileges.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- Attacker can view the source code (public repository or leaked config).\n\n```\ncookieSecret: \"[REDACTED-SECRET]\"\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nReplace the hardcoded secret with a value loaded from an environment variable or a secure secret management service. Remove the default value from the config file.\n\n**Exploitability:** Hardcoded session secret in config enables anyone with repository access to forge valid session cookies, completely bypassing authentication.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 9/10) \u2014 Hardcoded session secret in config/env/all.js flows through config/config.js into express-session middleware in server.js, with no environment-variable override in any deployment profile (production.js is empty). Anyone reading the public repo can forge session cookies for any user including admin.**"
          },
