            "description": "*2 additional call site(s) collapsed during dedup \u2014 same root cause; each location needs the same fix applied.*\n\n#### Description\nIn handleSignup, the raw password from req.body.password is passed directly to userDAO.addUser without any hashing or key derivation. The threat model and comments indicate bcrypt was intentionally omitted, so passwords are stored in plaintext.\n\n#### Impact\nIf the database is ever compromised, all passwords are immediately readable, exposing every user account to takeover.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAn attacker who obtains database access (e.g., via NoSQL injection elsewhere) can dump the user collection and read every password, gaining immediate access to all accounts.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- Attacker gains read access to the MongoDB database (e.g., through an injection vulnerability or misconfiguration).\n\n```\nuserDAO.addUser(userName, firstName, lastName, password, email, (err, user) => { ... });\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nHash passwords with bcrypt, argon2, or scrypt before calling addUser. Uncomment the bcrypt code in user-dao.js and adjust this call accordingly.\n\n**Exploitability:** Passwords stored in plaintext; a database breach exposes all user credentials, enabling full account takeover.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 Password from unauthenticated POST /signup \u2192 userDAO.addUser \u2192 MongoDB stored as plaintext (bcrypt fix intentionally commented out)",
