          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "security-severity": "4.6",
            "cvssRating": "Medium",
            "category": "CWE-601: URL Redirection to Untrusted Site (Open Redirect)",
            "cvssVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N",
            "cwe": "CWE-601 - URL Redirection to Untrusted Site (Open Redirect)",
            "cweId": "CWE-601",
            "cweName": "URL Redirection to Untrusted Site (Open Redirect)",
            "cvssScore": 4.6,
            "offensivePriority": "P3",
            "offensivePriorityLabel": "Internal Network / Privileged Position",
            "offensivePriorityReason": "Internal Network / Privileged Position | *exposure unverified \u2014 no CMDB context; AV:N (network-routable; internet exposure unconfirmed)*",
            "confidence": 0.99,
            "description": "#### Description\nThe /learn route handler extracts req.query.url directly and passes it to res.redirect() without any validation. No scheme, host, or allow-list check is performed, enabling redirection to any URL controlled by an attacker.\n\n#### Impact\nAn attacker can redirect any logged-in user to an arbitrary external site. This can be used in phishing attacks to steal credentials or trick users into downloading malware, leveraging the trust of the legitimate application domain.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAn attacker crafts a link such as https://example.com/learn?url=http://evil.com and distributes it to authenticated users. When a logged-in user clicks the link, the browser follows the redirect to the attacker's site, where a forged login page could harvest credentials.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- User must be authenticated (any session), which is easily obtainable in this training application.\n\n```\n    // Handle redirect for learning resources link\n    app.get(\"/learn\", isLoggedIn, (req, res) => {\n        // Insecure way to handle redirects by taking redirect url from query string\n        return res.redirect(req.query.url);\n    });\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nValidate redirect URLs using an allow-list of permitted hosts or enforce that the URL is a relative path. For example, check that url.startsWith('/') or match against a trusted domain before calling res.redirect().\n\n**Exploitability:** Open redirect via unvalidated req.query.url. Can be used in phishing campaigns to redirect users to attacker-controlled pages. Post-auth.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 req.query.url flows unsanitized into res.redirect() with no scheme/host/allow-list check; authenticated route, verified reachable via HTTP."
          },
