          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "security-severity": "5.3",
            "cvssRating": "Medium",
            "category": "CWE-204",
            "cvssVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N",
            "cwe": "CWE-204",
            "cweId": "CWE-204",
            "cvssScore": 5.3,
            "offensivePriority": "P3",
            "offensivePriorityLabel": "Internal Network / Privileged Position",
            "offensivePriorityReason": "Internal Network / Privileged Position | *exposure unverified \u2014 no CMDB context; AV:N (network-routable; internet exposure unconfirmed)*",
            "confidence": 1.0,
            "description": "#### Description\nThe login error handling returns 'Invalid username' for non-existent users and 'Invalid password' for existing users with wrong passwords. This differential response leaks valid usernames.\n\n#### Impact\nAn attacker can determine which usernames are registered in the system, enabling targeted password guessing or credential stuffing attacks.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAn attacker sends a series of POST requests to /login with candidate usernames and a dummy password. By observing whether the response says 'Invalid username' or 'Invalid password', they build a list of valid accounts.\n\n```\nif (err.noSuchUser) {\n    ...\n    loginError: invalidUserNameErrorMessage,\n} else if (err.invalidPassword) {\n    ...\n    loginError: invalidPasswordErrorMessage,\n}\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nChange the error responses to a generic message such as 'Invalid username or password' regardless of which credential is incorrect.\n\n**Exploitability:** Username enumeration via login error messages ('Invalid username' vs 'Invalid password'). Pre-auth, aids brute force.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 full chain verified: unauthenticated POST /login \u2192 validateLogin differential error \u2192 \"Invalid username\" vs \"Invalid password\" response leaks valid accounts"
          },
          "taxa": [
            {
              "toolComponent": {
                "name": "CWE",
                "guid": "b7c8d9e0-1f2a-3b4c-5d6e-7f8090a1b2c3"
              },
              "id": "CWE-204"
            }
          ],
          "rank": 53.0,
          "partialFingerprints": {
