        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-521",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Weak Password Complexity Requirement  [CVSS 6.5: CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N]"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/routes/session.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 144
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "security-severity": "6.5",
            "cvssRating": "Medium",
            "category": "CWE-521",
            "cvssVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N",
            "cwe": "CWE-521",
            "cweId": "CWE-521",
            "cvssScore": 6.5,
            "offensivePriority": "P3",
            "offensivePriorityLabel": "Internal Network / Privileged Position",
            "offensivePriorityReason": "Internal Network / Privileged Position | *exposure unverified \u2014 no CMDB context; AV:N (network-routable; internet exposure unconfirmed)*",
            "confidence": 1.0,
            "description": "#### Description\nThe signup validation uses PASS_RE = /^.{1,20}$/, which only enforces a length of 1\u201320 characters. It does not require mixed case, digits, or special characters.\n\n#### Impact\nUsers can set trivially weak passwords (e.g., a single character), making accounts highly susceptible to brute-force and dictionary attacks.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAfter enumerating a valid username, an attacker attempts common passwords (e.g., '123', 'password') until access is gained.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- Attacker must know or guess a valid username.\n\n```\nconst PASS_RE = /^.{1,20}$/;\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nReplace the weak regex with a stronger policy, e.g., /^(?=.*\\d)(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z]).{8,}$/, as shown in the commented-out fix.\n\n**Exploitability:** Weak password policy allows 1-20 char passwords with no complexity requirements. Pre-auth, enables credential guessing.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 Weak password regex /^.{1,20}$/ on unauthenticated POST /signup route; accepts 1-char passwords with no complexity. Stronger regex commented out. No compensating validation anywhere in the call chain."
          },
