            "cvssRating": "Medium",
            "category": "CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor",
            "cvssVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N",
            "cwe": "CWE-200 - Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor",
            "cweId": "CWE-200",
            "cweName": "Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor",
            "cvssScore": 5.3,
            "offensivePriority": "P3",
            "offensivePriorityLabel": "Internal Network / Privileged Position",
            "offensivePriorityReason": "Internal Network / Privileged Position | *exposure unverified \u2014 no CMDB context; AV:N (network-routable; internet exposure unconfirmed)*",
            "confidence": 0.95,
            "description": "#### Description\nWhen a new user submits a username that already exists, the signup handler replies with 'User name already in use. Please choose another'. This reveals valid usernames to an unauthenticated attacker.\n\n#### Impact\nAn attacker can enumerate existing usernames by attempting to create an account with a taken username and observing the unique error message.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\n1. Attacker submits POST /signup with a guessed username and other required fields. 2. If the response contains 'User name already in use', the username is registered.\n\n```\nerrors.userNameError = \"User name already in use. Please choose another\";\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nRespond with a generic message that does not reveal whether the username is already taken (e.g., 'Username is invalid or already taken').\n\n**Exploitability:** Username enumeration via signup error ('User name already in use'). Pre-auth, leaks valid usernames.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 unauthenticated POST /signup returns distinct error for existing usernames; no rate limiting or generic-error mitigation found"
          },
          "taxa": [
            {
              "toolComponent": {
                "name": "CWE",
                "guid": "b7c8d9e0-1f2a-3b4c-5d6e-7f8090a1b2c3"
