          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "security-severity": "6.5",
            "cvssRating": "Medium",
            "category": "CWE-1333: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity",
            "cvssVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
            "cwe": "CWE-1333 - Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity",
            "cweId": "CWE-1333",
            "cweName": "Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity",
            "cvssScore": 6.5,
            "offensivePriority": "P3",
            "offensivePriorityLabel": "Internal Network / Privileged Position",
            "offensivePriorityReason": "Internal Network / Privileged Position | *exposure unverified \u2014 no CMDB context; AV:N (network-routable; internet exposure unconfirmed)*",
            "confidence": 0.95,
            "description": "#### Description\nhandleProfileUpdate destructures bankRouting from req.body at line 49 and tests it against the regex /([0-9]+)+\\#/ at line 61. The nested quantifier ([0-9]+)+ is applied to user-controlled digits. When the input contains many digits but no terminating '#', the regex engine explores an exponential number of digit partitions before failing. No type check, length limit, or timeout exists before the vulnerable test.\n\n#### Impact\nA single authenticated request can cause exponential regex backtracking that ties up the Node.js event loop, making the entire application unresponsive for all users.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nLog in as any user. Submit a POST to /profile with bankRouting set to 30,000 digits followed by '!' (or any non-'#' suffix) and the other required body fields. The regex test on line 61 consumes CPU during catastrophic backtracking, blocking the event loop and denying service to other users.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- A valid user account (registration is open)\n\n```\nconst regexPattern = /([0-9]+)+\\#/;\nconst testComplyWithRequirements = regexPattern.test(bankRouting);\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nReplace the vulnerable regex with a linear anchored pattern such as /^[0-9]+#$/ or at least remove the outer '+' quantifier. Also validate that bankRouting is a string and enforce a short maximum length before testing.\n\n**Exploitability:** ReDoS in bankRouting regex allows denial of service. Requires authenticated request; can be used to degrade availability.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 Confirmed vulnerable regex on authenticated POST /profile with no upstream validation, length limit, or timeout."
          },
          "taxa": [
