          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "security-severity": "4.3",
            "cvssRating": "Medium",
            "category": "CWE-639: Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key",
            "cvssVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N",
            "cwe": "CWE-639 - Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key",
            "cweId": "CWE-639",
            "cweName": "Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key",
            "cvssScore": 4.3,
            "offensivePriority": "P3",
            "offensivePriorityLabel": "Internal Network / Privileged Position",
            "offensivePriorityReason": "Internal Network / Privileged Position | *exposure unverified \u2014 no CMDB context; AV:N (network-routable; internet exposure unconfirmed)*",
            "confidence": 0.95,
            "description": "#### Description\nThe displayMemos function extracts userId from req.session (line 22-24) but never passes it to memosDAO.getAllMemos (line 25). The callback renders ALL memos from the database into the view template (line 27-31). An attacker authenticated as any user can view memos created by other users, including those containing sensitive or private information.\n\n#### Impact\nAny authenticated user can view memos belonging to all users, not just their own. The getAllMemos function retrieves every memo in the database without filtering by the requesting user's ID, exposing potentially sensitive memo contents to unauthorized users.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\n1. Attacker registers or logs in as a low-privileged user. 2. Attacker navigates to the memos page. 3. The application displays all memos from the database, including those created by other users, because getAllMemos lacks a userId filter. The attacker can read any memo content that other users have stored.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- Attacker has a valid authenticated session (any user)\n\n```\nthis.displayMemos = (req, res, next) => {\n\n    const {\n        userId\n    } = req.session;\n\n    memosDAO.getAllMemos((err, docs) => {\n        if (err) return next(err);\n        return res.render(\"memos\", {\n            memosList: docs,\n            userId: userId,\n            environmentalScripts\n        });\n    });\n};\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nModify getAllMemos to accept a userId parameter and filter results. In displayMemos, pass req.session.userId to the DAO call: memosDAO.getAllMemos(userId, callback). Update the MemosDAO.getAllMemos implementation to query only memos where userId matches the provided parameter.\n\n**Exploitability:** IDOR in memos: any authenticated user can see all memos, regardless of owner. Post-auth.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 `getAllMemos` returns every document with no userId filter; the route is reachable by any authenticated user; no compensating control found."
          },
