            "description": "#### Description\nThe package.json pins swig to ^1.4.2 (line 22). Swig is officially unmaintained and deprecated with known security vulnerabilities in template compilation. The application explicitly sets autoescape: false in the Express configuration, meaning any user-controlled data rendered through Swig templates (such as profile fields, allocation data, memo content) will be emitted without HTML encoding. This creates a persistent XSS vector across multiple endpoints.\n\n#### Impact\nThe pinned Swig version 1.4.2 is unmaintained and contains unresolved security issues including potential for template injection when combined with application-level autoescape=false configuration.\n\n#### Exploit scenario\nAn attacker updates their profile bank routing number with an XSS payload like '111#&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;'. Because Swig with autoescape=false renders it without encoding, any viewer sees and executes the script.\n\n#### Preconditions\n- Application is configured with autoescape=false (confirmed in server.js configuration)\n\n```\n\"swig\": \"^1.4.2\"\n```\n\n#### How to fix\nReplace Swig with an actively maintained template engine like Nunjucks or Handlebars, or at minimum enable autoescaping. Since Swig is unmaintained, migration is strongly recommended.\n\n**Exploitability:** Unmaintained Swig template engine with autoescape=false globally. Any template-rendered user input is served without encoding, enabling XSS.\n\n#### Adversarial verification\n**Verdict:** TRUE_POSITIVE (confidence: 10/10) \u2014 autoescape:false confirmed in server.js; swig ^1.4.2 confirmed unmaintained; multiple external entry points render user data unencoded; zero compensating encoding defenses anywhere in the pipeline"
          },
